# Line endings, pinned rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# There was no file here, and this checkout has core.autocrlf=true, so the
# whole working tree is CRLF locally and LF in the repository. That works only
# for as long as everyone's config agrees. A clone with autocrlf=false commits
# CRLF back, and the next diff is the entire repository against itself.
#
# LF in the repository, everywhere. `uv.lock` matters most: uv writes it with
# LF and rewrites it wholesale, so a CRLF copy is a spurious conflict on every
# sync. A Makefile matters too -- make on macOS and Linux takes a trailing \r
# as part of the command and fails on recipes that are otherwise fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Scanner output and captures are gitignored today, but an ignore rule
# is not a promise: name them here so that a fixture added later cannot be
# corrupted by newline translation on the way in or out.
*.tif    -text
*.tiff   -text
*.npy    -text
*.npz    -text
*.bin    -text
*.gz     -text
*.png    -text
*.jpg    -text
*.jpeg   -text
*.pcapng -text
*.pcap   -text
